Z||000000||chris6878||09-12-1999||01:26 AM||||Hey...<P>I am currently rebuilding the engine in my 85 GT V6 and i noticed the transmission for the V6 looks similar to the transmission in my 84 model 4-banger. They are both auto. Do the 2.5 4cyl. and the 2.8 V6 have the same bolt up pattern to the tranny...<BR>you guys may thing i am dumb to ask this, but i am just curious...<P>Thanks in advance...<BR>Chris<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||SCCA FIERO||09-12-1999||01:45 AM||||The only dumb questions are the ones not asked. I myself was asking this same question a little while back.<P>Any Fiero motor will bolt to ANY Fiero tranny regardless if it's a V6 or I4. I bolted my Isuzu 5spd to my 2.8 V6 and stuffed it into my 88 coupe. (The Isuzu 5spd only came with 4 cylinder Fieros)||||reg||14
Z||000002||Kage86GT4SP||09-12-1999||05:08 AM||||SCCA,<P>I'm in the process of doing the same thing (Isuzu 5spd from an 85 4cyl to an 86 2.8 4spd) I have the 5 spd shifter, one of the two cables, and the tranny.  I plan on replacing all of the seals as a precaution.<P>Do I need to get different tranny mounts? Will the 4spd mounts work? And is there any way to use the same cables?  Is there anything special I need to look out for when doing this swap?<P>Thanx!  <P>K.<BR>  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||chris6878||09-12-1999||11:07 AM||||WOW....   I thought there was a similarity between the trannys. Will the 5-speed 4-cyl tranny hold up the the HP put out by the V6??<P>Thanks alot guys||||reg||1
Z||000004||chris6878||09-12-1999||11:12 AM||||Hey...   <P>What years did the fiero come out with the 5-speed?    thanks again<P>chris||||reg||5
Z||000005||theogre||09-12-1999||11:33 AM||||As I recall, GM had reliability problems with the 5 speed when used on the V6. That was why they never came factory. At least that was what I remember about what the car rags where told when they asked GM why the 5 speed was unavailable..... As I understand, The V6 was never available with that izusu tranny in any GM car.<P>The automatic is TH-125c in all Fiero and all 4cyl & V6 GM cars using 3spd auto trans. The only dif may be in the size of the apply pistons. The bigger motor may have slightly larger bore pistons.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 09-12-1999).]||||reg||5
Z||000006||Standard||09-13-1999||02:06 AM||||Chris, the 86 4 cyl and 86.5 v6 were the first models with the v6||||reg||3
Z||000007||chris6878||09-14-1999||01:06 AM||||Thanks Guys...||||reg||14
Z||000008||bHooper||09-14-1999||11:20 AM||||Yes, I would like to know about the transmission mounts myself.||||reg||10
Z||000009||SCCA FIERO||09-14-1999||02:14 PM||||The tranny mounts appear to have different part #s and they do not look the same. When I swapped my motor the tranny stayed in the car and I just used the tranny mounts that were already there. According to the P car parts and Illustration book, they use different mounts. If you are able to locate the tranny you want to swap in, maybe the mounts will be included. ||||reg||4
